# The resource pack is a build artefact as much as source: the committed
# files are zipped and served to clients against a published SHA-1, so their
# bytes must not change between checkouts. Without this, Git's autocrlf on
# Windows rewrites the JSON line endings and the zip built from a fresh clone
# no longer matches the hash in the README.
*.json text eol=lf
*.mcmeta text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Binary assets - never touched.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
